DTSTAMP:20261128T033928Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270102
SUMMARY:Mamdani's first year in office
DESCRIPTION:One year since the inaugural address of Jan. 1\, 2026. A cust
 omary peg for retrospectives rather than a scheduled event.
CATEGORIES:cityhall
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20270116-Preliminarybudgetforfiscal2028@nyc-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261128T033928Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270116
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270117
SUMMARY:Preliminary budget for fiscal 2028
DESCRIPTION:Mamdani's second budget\, due under Charter section 236. Note
  the February deadline does not apply: the extension exists only in the 
 year following a mayoral election\, which was 2026.\n\nhttps://codelibra
 ry.amlegal.com/codes/newyorkcity/latest/NYCcharter/0-0-0-1
URL:https://codelibrary.amlegal.com/codes/newyorkcity/latest/NYCcharter/0
 -0-0-1
CATEGORIES:budget
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20270201-Stateexecutivebudgetdue@nyc-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261128T033928Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270202
SUMMARY:State executive budget due
DESCRIPTION:In the year following a gubernatorial election\, the state co
 nstitution requires the governor's budget by Feb. 1. It determines city 
 tax authority\, transit funding and Medicaid cost-sharing.\n\nhttps://ww
 w.budget.ny.gov/
URL:https://www.budget.ny.gov/
CATEGORIES:budget
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20270401-Statebudgetdue@nyc-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261128T033928Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270401
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270402
SUMMARY:State budget due
DESCRIPTION:The state constitution requires a budget by April 1. It gates
  the money for child care and for fare-free buses\, and it is the realis
 tic vehicle for any millionaire or corporate tax increase\, all of which
  require Albany.\n\nhttps://www.nysenate.gov/new-york-state-budget
URL:https://www.nysenate.gov/new-york-state-budget
CATEGORIES:power
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20270501-Executivebudgetforfiscal2028@nyc-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261128T033928Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270501
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270502
SUMMARY:Executive budget for fiscal 2028
DESCRIPTION:The mayor's revised budget\, due under Charter section 249\, 
 updated for whatever Albany did on April 1.\n\nhttps://codelibrary.amleg
 al.com/codes/newyorkcity/latest/NYCcharter/0-0-0-1
URL:https://codelibrary.amlegal.com/codes/newyorkcity/latest/NYCcharter/0
 -0-0-1
CATEGORIES:budget
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20270624-RentGuidelinesBoardfinalvote@nyc-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261128T033928Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270624
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270625
SUMMARY:Rent Guidelines Board final vote
DESCRIPTION:The rent adjustment for roughly a million rent-stabilized apa
 rtments\, for leases beginning October 2027. Date estimated from recent 
 practice (June 17\, 2024\; June 30\, 2025\; June 25\, 2026).\n\nhttps://
 rentguidelinesboard.cityofnewyork.us/
URL:https://rentguidelinesboard.cityofnewyork.us/
CATEGORIES:housing
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20270630-Fiscal2028budgetadoption@nyc-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261128T033928Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270630
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270701
SUMMARY:Fiscal 2028 budget adoption
DESCRIPTION:The Charter's trigger date is June 5 (section 254)\, but in p
 ractice adoption lands at the end of June: the fiscal 2027 deal was stru
 ck and voted on June 30\, 2026\, hours before the deadline. Date estimat
 ed from that practice.\n\nhttps://council.nyc.gov/budget/
URL:https://council.nyc.gov/budget/
CATEGORIES:budget
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20280101-FiveboroughsconsolidateintoGreaterNewYor@nyc-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261128T033928Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20280101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20280102
SUMMARY:Five boroughs consolidate into Greater New York — 130th anniversa
 ry
DESCRIPTION:On New Year's Day 1898 Manhattan\, Brooklyn\, Queens\, the Br
 onx and Staten Island merged into a single city of more than three milli
 on people.\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/City_of_Greater_New_York
URL:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/City_of_Greater_New_York
CATEGORIES:anniversary
END:VEVENT
